      "parsed_output": {
        "files_changed": [
          "obr/src/main/java/org/apache/karaf/obr/command/util/FileUtil.java",
          "obr/src/test/java/org/apache/karaf/obr/command/util/FileUtilTest.java"
        ],
        "patch_notes": "Root cause: FileUtil.unjar() derived `destName`/`destDir` from the (attacker-controlled) JAR entry name and passed them to FileUtil.copy(), which built the final output file (`new File(targetDir, destName)`, the sink at old line 171) with NO containment check of its own — it only relied on a check performed earlier in unjar() on a differently-constructed File object (`target = new File(dir, je.getName())`). That made copy() unsafe both when called directly (it's a public method) and, more subtly, because its own resolved path was never verified. In addition, the pre-existing unjar() check used a raw `String.startsWith()` comparison of canonical paths without a trailing separator, which is vulnerable to the classic sibling-directory bypass (e.g. dest `target/test` vs an entry resolving to `target/testEVIL/...`, which also \"starts with\" `target/test`).\n\nFix:\n1. In FileUtil.copy() (the actual extraction sink), compute the fully resolved `targetFile` and its canonical path, then verify it equals the destination directory's canonical path or starts with `canonicalDir + File.separator` before creating any directories or writing the file. This closes the gap for both traces in the alert (both terminate at the `new File(...)`/FileOutputStream sink in copy()) and protects any current or future caller of copy(), not just unjar().\n2. Hardened the existing containment check in FileUtil.unjar() the same way (append `File.separator` to the prefix comparison, plus an equals check) to eliminate the sibling-directory prefix bypass as defense in depth.\n3. Added regression tests: `badExtractSiblingPrefixTest` (unjar sibling-prefix bypass) and `badCopyDirectTest` (calling copy() directly with a `..`-laden destDir) alongside the existing `badExtractTest`/`goodExtractTest`.\n\nNo behavioral change for legitimate archives whose entries resolve inside the destination directory.",
        "regression_commands": [
          "cd obr && mvn -B test -Dtest=FileUtilTest",
          "cd obr && mvn -B test"
        ],
        "risk_notes": "Low risk: the change only adds a containment check before writes in copy() and tightens an existing check in unjar(); it does not alter behavior for well-formed archives. IOException is already a declared/handled exception type in both methods, so the new failure path fits existing error handling (downloadSource() catches Exception and prints the error). Ran `mvn clean test -Dtest=FileUtilTest` in the project's Docker container: 4/4 tests pass (2 pre-existing + 2 new).",
        "status": "patched",
        "summary": "Fixed CWE-022 path traversal in OBR's FileUtil archive extraction by enforcing canonical-path containment at the actual write sink (copy()) and hardening the existing check in unjar() against a prefix-matching bypass."
      }
    }
  ],
